--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -19,3 +19,21 @@ resolvePointer({ a: 1 }, ""); // the whole document
 It throws a `JsonPointerError` when the pointer is not valid (not a string, no leading `/`, or a `~` not
 followed by `0` or `1`) or when it does not resolve to a value of the document (missing member, array index
 out of range or not canonical, `-`, or descending into a scalar). Only own members of objects are considered.
+
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` (RFC 6902) applies an array of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and
+`test` operations, in order, and returns the resulting document as a new value; the inputs are not mutated:
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyPatch({ foo: ["bar"] }, [
+  { op: "add", path: "/foo/-", value: "baz" },
+  { op: "test", path: "/foo/1", value: "baz" },
+]); // { foo: ["bar", "baz"] }
+```
+
+It throws when the patch is invalid (not an array, unknown `op`, missing `value` or `from`, bad pointer) or when
+an operation fails (missing target, array index out of range, failed `test`, removing the whole document,
+moving a value into its own child).
