index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7a922cab8b332e782e89d6fea1606dc26adb3642
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-add-json-patch/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/index.ts` already has `resolvePointer` and a private `parsePointer` (RFC 6901) that throws `JsonPointerError`. Pointer resolution is read-only; patching needs parent lookup and mutation.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** RFC 6902 conformance for all six operations; no mutation of inputs; errors for invalid patches and failed operations.
+**Non-Goals:** merge patch, diff, in-place API.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Deep-clone the document first (`structuredClone`), clone `value`s on insertion, then mutate the clone with a small helper. This guarantees input isolation, and failure leaves the input intact.
+- Reuse `parsePointer` for `path`/`from`; add `JsonPatchError` for patch-level failures. Pointer syntax errors propagate as `JsonPointerError`.
+- Parent lookup walks tokens with the same rules as `resolvePointer` (own members only, canonical indices, no `-` on read); the final token is interpreted per operation (`-` and index == length allowed only for `add`).
+- `move` = `remove` + `add` on the working copy, with the proper-prefix check done on token arrays. Same-location move is a no-op.
+- `test` uses a recursive deep-equal that is order-insensitive for objects and type-strict.
+- Own-member checks use `Object.hasOwn`; assigning keys such as `__proto__` uses `Object.defineProperty` to avoid prototype pollution.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Cloning cost is O(document size) per call; accepted for safety.
+- RFC leaves root `remove` undefined; we throw.
