@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Why
+
+Services need to update JSON documents with standard patches. The library already resolves JSON Pointers (RFC 6901) but cannot apply JSON Patch (RFC 6902).
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, supporting `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+- It returns a new document and never mutates its input; it throws when the patch is invalid or an operation fails.
+- Out of scope: JSON Merge Patch, patch generation (diff), and in-place application.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 JSON Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts` gains a new export; `src/index.test.ts` gains tests; README documents the function. No dependencies.
